# Cursor AI Rules for Spotify A/B Testing Project

## Project Context
You are working on a production-grade A/B testing framework for Spotify playlist optimization using LLMs. The project uses Python 3.13+, SQLite for data storage, Hugging Face Transformers for NLP, and Streamlit for dashboards.

## Code Style Guidelines
- Use type hints for all functions
- Write comprehensive docstrings in NumPy style
- Follow Black formatting (88 char line length)
- Prefer pandas method chaining over intermediate variables
- SQL queries should use CTEs over subqueries
- Always use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection

## Common Patterns
- DataFrames are imported as: import pandas as pd
- Use pathlib.Path over os.path
- Logging over print statements
- F-strings over .format() or %

## Testing Requirements
- Every function needs a corresponding test
- Use pytest fixtures for test data
- Mock external API calls
- Aim for >80% code coverage

## Performance Considerations
- Vectorize operations instead of loops
- Use chunking for large datasets
- Cache expensive computations
- Profile before optimizing

## Project-Specific Context
- Skip rate is the primary metric (lower is better)
- Session length is secondary metric (higher is better)
- Always consider statistical significance
- Business impact > statistical significance
